 abbrev TPos (G : PlusSlicedCertificate Γ Del) : Type := G.Pos × ℤ
 
+/-! ## The position-space leaf cache
+
+`verts` filters `Finset.univ ×ˢ winTimes` by `v.1 ∈ posAt v.2`, which calls `posAt` once per
+PAIR although only `|winTimes|` distinct times occur — 512 calls where 6 would do, at a
+width-2 certificate over four window times. `posTable` tabulates `posAt` over the window
+extended one step each way, which is what `nextTime` / `prevTime` can reach.
+
+`posAtC` falls back to `posAt` itself off the table's range. That is what makes `posAtC_eq`
+**unconditional**: there is no side condition, so no use site can observe a difference and
+nothing below this module is ever accepted on the cache's authority.
+
+The table is bound in a `let` **outside** each filter lambda, and this is a correctness
+condition on the optimisation rather than a stylistic choice. A plain `posAtC v.2` call per pair
+re-runs `G.posTable` on every call — it is a function application, not a value — and rebuilds
+the whole table 512 times; measured at a width-2 certificate that form is **6.2x slower than no
+cache at all**, while the `let`-bound form is 74x faster. The `let` is the optimisation.
+
+The lookup compares with `==` rather than through a `Decidable` instance on `=`: this namespace
+already has a `decide` (`DecisionProcedure.lean`'s, on `Formula`), which shadows the core one.
+-/
+
+/-- `posAt` tabulated over the window times extended one step each way. -/
+def posTable (G : PlusSlicedCertificate Γ Del) : List (ℤ × Finset G.Pos) :=
+  (List.range (G.winHi - G.winLo + 2).toNat).map fun i =>
+    (G.winLo - 1 + (i : ℤ), G.posAt (G.winLo - 1 + (i : ℤ)))
+
+/-- The cached position space, with `posAt` itself as the off-range fallback. -/
+def posAtC (G : PlusSlicedCertificate Γ Del) (t : ℤ) : Finset G.Pos :=
+  match G.posTable.find? (fun p => p.1 == t) with
+  | some p => p.2
+  | none => G.posAt t
+
+/-- **The cache is the function**, with no side condition — every table entry is literally
+`(s, G.posAt s)`, and off the table the lookup *is* `posAt`. -/
+theorem posAtC_eq (G : PlusSlicedCertificate Γ Del) (t : ℤ) : G.posAtC t = G.posAt t := by
+  unfold posAtC
+  split
+  · rename_i p h
+    have hmem : p ∈ G.posTable := List.mem_of_find?_eq_some h
+    have hbeq := List.find?_some h
+    have heq : p.1 = t := by simpa using hbeq
+    rw [posTable, List.mem_map] at hmem
+    obtain ⟨i, _, hi⟩ := hmem
+    subst hi
+    simp only at heq ⊢
+    rw [heq]
+  · rfl
+
